SOAPBOX: This year's effort ended up to be little over 6 hrs of operating time
SOAPBOX: and 80m band only. As always in any CQ WW leg or any contest, quality
SOAPBOX: of signals is sometimes very varied and left to be desired. On many
SOAPBOX: occasions I got someone CQing very close to my QRG resulting in losing
SOAPBOX: few QSOs. Usualy sending PSE UP QSY resulted in nothing and pretending
SOAPBOX: of me not being heard. What a surprise when LY7Z did same and after
SOAPBOX: single polite PSE QSY then sent sri and moved. What a ham spirit! Well
SOAPBOX: done. Anyway I did little less than 7 hours of total operating on 80m
SOAPBOX: only. Used Flex 6300, 3 el phased array on TX and 6 Beverages on RX,
SOAPBOX: NCC-2 and LZ1AQ Loops for EU. Verticals were not the best for working
SOAPBOX: into EU I guess and perhaps that was reason why I got "jumped". Next
SOAPBOX: year I put Inv-V and will run 100W into it paralel. PA: Homebrew
SOAPBOX: 4GU81m / triode strap.
CREATED-BY: Win-Test 4.58.0
